(Chapter 1  What is machine learning) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Machine learning is a branch of artificial intelligence that lets computers) Tj
T*
(learn from data instead of following a fixed set of rules written by a) Tj
T*
(developer. The developer gives the program examples and a goal, and the) Tj
T*
(program finds the patterns that reach that goal by itself.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(There are three common types. Supervised learning uses labelled examples,) Tj
T*
(such as emails already marked as spam or not spam. Unsupervised learning) Tj
T*
(finds hidden groups in data that has no labels. Reinforcement learning) Tj
T*
(trains an agent with rewards for good actions and penalties for bad ones.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A model starts with random guesses. It predicts, measures the error) Tj
T*
(against the correct answer, and adjusts its internal numbers a little.) Tj
T*
(This loop repeats thousands of times until the error becomes small.) Tj
T*
