T*
() Tj
T*
(Retrieval augmented generation, short RAG, searches your own documents) Tj
T*
(before the language model answers, so the answer can be based on real) Tj
T*
(evidence instead of the model's memory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The first step is loading. A document loader reads a file and returns) Tj
T*
(Document objects. Each Document has page_content, the text itself, and) Tj
T*
(metadata, which describes where the text came from.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The second step is splitting. A text splitter cuts the big document into) Tj
T*
(small pieces called chunks, because embedding models work with small) Tj
T*
(pieces of text. Chunk size and chunk overlap control how the cuts are) Tj
T*
(made. Overlap repeats a little text so that a sentence crossing a cut is) Tj
T*
(still understandable in both neighbouring chunks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Each chunk then becomes an embedding, a list of numbers that represents) Tj
T*
(its meaning, and the embeddings are stored in a vector database. A) Tj
T*
(question is embedded the same way and the closest chunks are retrieved.) Tj
T*
